BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 792.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 780.00 Td (TIME-TRAVEL CLI v1.4 - DEDUP + CRYPTO CORE) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 768.00 Td (Pure C11 engine. Static binary. Linux only.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 756.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 732.00 Td ("Serious versioning for those who want Ctrl+Z across their entire project.") Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 708.00 Td (Language:    C11 \(engine and CLI\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 696.00 Td (Binary:      Static CLI \(musl-gcc + integrated xdelta3, BLAKE2b and crypto\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 684.00 Td (             Zero runtime dependencies.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 672.00 Td (Format:      TTDLTA01, packed little-endian records with xdelta3 deltas.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 660.00 Td (             Optional XChaCha20-Poly1305 payload encryption.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 648.00 Td (             Optional BLAKE2b content-addressed 64 KiB dedup blocks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 636.00 Td (Status:      Production. Core validated with 116/116 assertions across 43 sections.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 624.00 Td (             Functional battery: 108 assertions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 612.00 Td (             Dedicated Valgrind memory audit: 8 assertions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 600.00 Td (             TSan mode evaluates the 108 functional assertions and skips the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 588.00 Td (             Valgrind memory audit automatically.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 564.00 Td (v1.4:        DEDUP + ENCRYPTION.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 552.00 Td (             Files >= 1 MiB can be captured as 64 KiB BLAKE2b) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 540.00 Td (             content-addressed blocks. Repos can be encrypted with) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 528.00 Td (             XChaCha20-Poly1305. Adds store verification, atomic) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 516.00 Td (             compaction, orphan-block GC and hardened failure paths.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 492.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 480.00 Td (DEVELOPMENT AND TESTING ENVIRONMENT) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 468.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 456.00 Td (All code and the 116-assertion / 43-section regression battery were developed and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 444.00 Td (validated on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 432.00 Td (following hardware, without access to modern machines during the process:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 408.00 Td (CPU:       Intel Core 2 Duo T7500 @ 2.20 GHz \(2 cores, year 2007\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 396.00 Td (OS:        Linux Mint 21 x86_64 \(kernel 5.15 LTS\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 384.00 Td (RAM:       4 GB) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 372.00 Td (Disk:      Mechanical HDD \(no SSD\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 360.00 Td (Toolchain: musl-gcc, gcc sanitizer builds, xdelta3, Valgrind) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 336.00 Td (Key results on this hardware:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 312.00 Td (- 108 functional regression assertions passing in normal mode.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 300.00 Td (- 116/116 assertions passing when the dedicated Valgrind memory audit is included.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 288.00 Td (- TSan mode: 108 evaluated assertions + 1 skipped Valgrind section.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 276.00 Td (- AddressSanitizer / UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer audit builds available.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 264.00 Td (- ThreadSanitizer audit build available.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 252.00 Td (- Valgrind memory audit: 0 leaks, 0 errors.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 240.00 Td (- Atomic restoration via temp+rename: zero partial writes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 228.00 Td (- Store verification detects corrupted or tampered .ttd files, including invalid magic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 216.00 Td (- Dedup restore validated with 2 MiB random files.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 204.00 Td (- Dedup GC removes orphan blocks while preserving referenced blocks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 192.00 Td (- Encrypted stores leave no plaintext in .ttd files.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 180.00 Td (- Encrypted compact leaves no plaintext behind.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 168.00 Td (- Wrong passphrase does not modify or garbage-collect dedup blocks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 156.00 Td (- Corrupted dedup blocks are detected during restore.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 144.00 Td (- Corrupted crypto.meta is rejected.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 120.00 Td (If it works here, it works anywhere.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 96.00 Td (NOTE: All times mentioned were measured in the environment described above.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 84.00 Td (On modern hardware \(NVMe SSD, multi-core CPU\), results are orders of) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 72.00 Td (magnitude better.) Tj ET
endstream
