BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 792.00 Td (Factors:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 780.00 Td (- Delta encoding: small changes produce small deltas \(~20-30 bytes for a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 768.00 Td (  line edit in a 600-byte file\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 756.00 Td (- Full copies: very small files \(<~50 bytes\) are always stored as full) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 744.00 Td (  CREATE because deltas are larger.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 732.00 Td (- Compaction: collapses long delta chains into base + super-delta.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 720.00 Td (- Binary files: photos, videos, compressed archives don't generate good) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 708.00 Td (  deltas; each version stores almost the full size.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 684.00 Td (To check current usage:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 672.00 Td (    timetravel status --repo /path/to/project) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 648.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 636.00 Td (16.4 CAN I BACKUP THE .TIMETRAVEL DIRECTORY?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 624.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 612.00 Td (YES, but it's not recommended. The .timetravel directory contains all) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 600.00 Td (history. Backing it up creates a circular dependency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 576.00 Td (Better approach: backup the SOURCE files with a traditional tool \(BareSnap,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 564.00 Td (rsync, tar\). The .timetravel store is a local undo buffer, not a backup.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 540.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 528.00 Td (16.5 WHAT HAPPENS IF THE DAEMON CRASHES?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 516.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 504.00 Td (The store is NEVER left in a corrupt state:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 492.00 Td (- Records are written atomically \(all or nothing\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 480.00 Td (- Without fsync per record, some recent records might be lost on power) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 468.00 Td (  loss, but existing records remain intact.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 456.00 Td (- On restart, the daemon rebuilds its cache from disk and continues.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 444.00 Td (- The PID file is cleaned on graceful exit; obsolete PIDs are detected via) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 432.00 Td (  kill\(pid, 0\) and overwritten on new startup.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 408.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 396.00 Td (16.6 CAN TWO DAEMONS WATCH THE SAME DIRECTORY?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 384.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 372.00 Td (NO. In v1.3 there is only ever ONE daemon \(the monolith\). A second `start`) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 360.00 Td (or `add` detects the running monolith via the boot lock + IPC discovery and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 348.00 Td (joins it instead of spawning a duplicate. Concurrent startups are) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 336.00 Td (serialized so exactly one daemon is created. Overlapping repos are rejected.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 312.00 Td (Use `timetravel stop --repo <dir>` to detach a repo, or plain `stop` to halt) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 300.00 Td (the whole monolith.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 276.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 264.00 Td (16.7 CAN I WATCH SEVERAL UNRELATED FOLDERS AT ONCE?  \(NEW IN V1.3\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 252.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 240.00 Td (YES. This is the headline feature of v1.3. Start the monolith with one) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 228.00 Td (folder and attach the rest hot:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 216.00 Td (    timetravel start ~/src) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 204.00 Td (    timetravel add ~/docs) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 192.00 Td (    timetravel add /mnt/data/notes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 168.00 Td (Each folder keeps its own isolated .timetravel store. Inspect the whole) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 156.00 Td (swarm at any time with plain `timetravel status`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 132.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 120.00 Td (16.8 IS THERE ENCRYPTION?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 108.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 84.00 Td (YES, starting with v1.4.) Tj ET
endstream
